  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_b7e5e6c984024ba189284c0711a001a2",
      "statement": "`align_citations(answer, sources)` is the basic entry point; it accepts plain `str`, `SourceDocument`, and `SourceChunk` items (mixed in one call) and returns `list[SpanCitations]`, one per answer segment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L72-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f951b3e77d98a52114d2e7c251e6763abf4de2ebfeb7198c2bdaeaf08e58282e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L399-L435",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9112fab59b0aff42fa7dcf2901527a6aeebafb3becc7f42d1f80d2d23a32489b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_00c933e693974435b8ccf72779a5f9ca",
      "statement": "Each `SpanCitations` carries `answer_span` (with half-open `char_start`/`char_end` into the answer), a ranked `citations` list, a `retrieval_support` list of passages the selector picked up that did not localize, and a `status` literal of exactly `\"supported\"`, `\"partial\"`, or `\"unsupported\"`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/results.py#L165-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83dbe574b13fa18f29d53f39eaf0179129939929f26eb00b2c7bd2a80e23f2cc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/results.py#L302-L348",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:06e0230233700c5999dbcd6f7b08193939225cc097a8f7c967d351d762022fe5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6ac885360c1c4c9bb87e22b827f81ed1",
      "statement": "All `Citation` and `EvidenceSpan` offsets are Python half-open intervals into the source document, and after chunk rebasing `source.text[citation.char_start:citation.char_end] == citation.evidence`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/results.py#L111-L162",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af562243ab05fb1a0ca7bdfbd1bb27de39bf7e78d2b5353e48125ef2070f3231:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/results.py#L212-L283",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bcc38446911239862623829b957c48de7f8913d48f84198f52290b1245742b36:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7fd6bcef698b4a35b315c22f588aa8fb",
      "statement": "Status is computed by `_span_status` from the best exact `Citation`'s `answer_coverage` (never from embedding similarity): `\"supported\"` requires `answer_coverage >= supported_answer_coverage` (default 0.6) and a clean contradiction check; `\"partial\"` means citations exist but coverage is below that threshold, or the contradiction check fired; `\"unsupported\"` means no citation survived filtering. The literal is exactly `\"partial\"`, never `\"partially_supported\"`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1610-L1633",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0546591f2ac5ef2ec8353fa6d983babe6920c357814b4eae7d76a64a8120f7ff:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L25-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d0efb8731a7c4f15466c007a885166c612ef2e964877a33c8ac488efbdc366f0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c58706174f0b4629a667667ae2df3008",
      "statement": "The contradiction check (negation, number, leftover n-gram slot, entity swap, temporal/polarity markers) downgrades a span to `\"partial\"` (not `\"unsupported\"`) when it fires, because the evidence exists and only conflicts with the claim; the check runs against the full candidate passage, not the truncated Smith-Waterman evidence.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1592-L1633",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d926bf2abbb6d64eec30e23c480657e1d76d645551983135a3bad39420dd774c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/contradiction.py#L1-L285",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f39aab1f7ef9f7e5249699543e387176d37c3e66dcca33de28e5ccd4a8a04da2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a54ca78c88f24210afd6f99d0877daa2",
      "statement": "`retrieval_support` entries are passages the index or embedder selected that did not localize into a `Citation`; they are informational and never change the per-span status. A high embedding score that never localizes is `retrieval_support`, not a `Citation`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1610-L1633",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0546591f2ac5ef2ec8353fa6d983babe6920c357814b4eae7d76a64a8120f7ff:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/results.py#L286-L299",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28ad5eaf6616340d4a57fc96a6729eb589345afa5becdd34613b17bc3641b64a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3741e0feef9d4f4684cd7c38a1b2bab5",
      "statement": "`PreparedCitationCorpus.from_sources` builds the inverted index on the default / Rust path (with `SimpleTokenizer` and `SimpleSegmenter`); when the Rust extension is missing or a custom tokenizer/segmenter is supplied, it leaves `inverted_index=None` and the candidate selector falls back to lexical prefilter. The public API and resulting `status` values are the same on both paths.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L101-L292",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4411147fea20e024971620a8dc8768661d3776aaa25bf3dffdcee92c67a0cd1e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0769a6e191df46f5a2d86d26840f0266",
      "statement": "When an `Embedder` is passed to `PreparedCitationCorpus.from_sources`, an embedding index is built on top of the prepared candidates; `_add_embedding_candidates` can add non-index windows to the candidate set, those extras still go through Smith-Waterman, and embedding-only `retrieval_support` still respects `min_embedding_similarity` (default 0.3).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L60-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b9398fa6a00420be24d88f510ae63eab470e4c887b0b4f09ea9a2506ea118c8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L270-L292",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8073ec1f2de16e634015215dc4850475f986fd614cf982d9162501d16c01f47b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a10fb9eb698645889d21f37c456fa4d1",
      "statement": "A `Citation`'s `score` is a weighted sum of components in `Citation.components`; `components[\"answer_coverage\"]` is the fraction of answer tokens matched by the alignment and is the value that drives `status`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1610-L1633",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0546591f2ac5ef2ec8353fa6d983babe6920c357814b4eae7d76a64a8120f7ff:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/results.py#L212-L283",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bcc38446911239862623829b957c48de7f8913d48f84198f52290b1245742b36:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1bf42209281e485bb733620cffa3fb23",
      "statement": "`CitationConfig.top_k` (default 3) caps how many exact `Citation` objects are returned per answer span, and `max_citations_per_source` (default 2) caps how many a single source can contribute to one span. `retrieval_support` is independently trimmed to `max_retrieval_support` (default 3).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L55-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2415ac4a547a7ce7eb1517a7a4aae4322d1ecd04b6e61a60764310d78f59a4c5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fc2c500c951f4d34818ce3a33f5e1e5e",
      "statement": "Multi-sentence answers are segmented first; the default `SimpleAnswerSegmenter` splits on sentence boundaries and `SpacyAnswerSegmenter` can split coordinated clauses. Each segment is processed independently and carries its own `answer_span` with `char_start`/`char_end` back into the full answer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L294-L364",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4cafe72a14a922233b8cb59018b3d91cb8fc9242699fb2b93dc17b8c9bb80303:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/results.py#L165-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83dbe574b13fa18f29d53f39eaf0179129939929f26eb00b2c7bd2a80e23f2cc:"
        }
      ]
    }
